From 5fce4c1a8de0c977193ced4fcba31809630b1b94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:18:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HexKagune 4.1.1: no structure in water

- Every structure checks the land under it and 8 blocks round it: no wet biome
  (hexkagune:wet: seas, rivers, beaches, swamps) every 4 blocks, no water over the
  ground every 16 (village/DryLand, pure and tested).
- The Aogiri hideout: its structure set is a random spread; the world's one hideout is
  built only at the nearest offer on dry land in its biomes (DryLand.hideoutOffers and
  choose, worked out once per world in ControlStructures.Site.hideout). It used to be
  built at its ring's spot whatever the ground (the sea floor).
- The villages try up to 9 spots within their start chunk's reach. Anteiku, the library
  and Ken's tower are a new type, hexkagune:dry_place: the vanilla jigsaw moved a chunk
  at a time (up to 5) to dry land, kept within reach.
- API allowlist: GenerationContext's constructor and accessors, GenerationStub,
  StructurePiecesBuilder and BoundingBox accessors, BiomeSource.getNoiseBiome,
  RandomState.sampler, Holder.is, TagKey.create, Registries.BIOME. Protocol 110.
- NpcTests: the columns' cover, lakes, wet patches and rivers anywhere, the game's
  spread written out, the hideout's choice, every structure's type.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018kcYHECCipSV28FpRzFLbh
